+# MikuOS has no descriptor passing over a Unix socket, which ipc-channel's
+# unix backend is built on; its in-process backend compiles everywhere. What
+# that costs: `zed <path>` from a second process cannot hand the path to a
+# running Zed (the CLI's channel), so each launch is its own instance
+[target.'cfg(target_os = "miku")'.dependencies]
